Argument:
  (<Game code>)

Description:
  This command starts classic text adventures in Z-machine format using
  Frotz. If the command is entered without an argument, a list of all
  adventures installed on the system is displayed.

  Each game has a game code which is entered after the command.

  Example:
    Adventure stugan

  starts the game Stugan.

Note:
  The available games are selected by the SysOp. Only games which are
  both registered in SklaffKOM and have an installed story file are
  shown in the game list.

Background:
  The Z-machine was originally created by Infocom for their text
  adventures. Rather than writing every game directly for a particular
  computer, the games were written for a virtual machine. The same story
  file could therefore run on many completely different computers, as
  long as a Z-machine interpreter was available.

  That turned out to be a rather good idea. Several decades later, the
  same old games can still be played on modern systems.

  SklaffKOM uses Frotz as its Z-machine interpreter. This means that both
  classic Infocom games and much newer works of interactive fiction can
  be played directly from the BBS.
